---
layout: layouts/base.njk
---

{% if heroImage %}
<section class="hero-section min-h-[400px] md:min-h-[500px]" style="background-image: url('{{ heroImage }}');"></section>
{% endif %}

<section class="bg-white py-12">
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 md:px-8 text-center">
    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-heading text-mascp-dark mb-4 pb-2 border-b-2 border-mascp-terracotta inline-block">FAIR TRADE/CHALATE ARTS</h1>
    {% if introText %}
    <p class="text-base md:text-lg leading-relaxed text-mascp-dark mt-8">{{ introText }}</p>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
</section>

<section class="bg-white">
  <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 md:px-8 pb-12">
    <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row gap-8">

      <div class="md:w-2/5">
        {% if mainText %}
        <div class="prose text-base md:text-lg leading-relaxed text-mascp-dark mb-4">
          {{ mainText | markdownify | safe }}
        </div>
        {% endif %}
        <a href="/donate/" class="btn-primary inline-block">Donate Now</a>
      </div>

      <div class="md:w-3/5">
        <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); gap: 8px;">
          {% if galleryImage1 %}<img src="{{ galleryImage1 }}" alt="" style="width: 100%; height: 200px; object-fit: cover;">{% endif %}
          {% if galleryImage2 %}<img src="{{ galleryImage2 }}" alt="" style="width: 100%; height: 200px; object-fit: cover;">{% endif %}
          {% if galleryImage3 %}<img src="{{ galleryImage3 }}" alt="" style="width: 100%; height: 200px; object-fit: cover;">{% endif %}
          {% if galleryImage4 %}<img src="{{ galleryImage4 }}" alt="" style="width: 100%; height: 200px; object-fit: cover;">{% endif %}
          {% if galleryImage5 %}<img src="{{ galleryImage5 }}" alt="" style="width: 100%; height: 200px; object-fit: cover;">{% endif %}
          {% if galleryImage6 %}<img src="{{ galleryImage6 }}" alt="" style="width: 100%; height: 200px; object-fit: cover;">{% endif %}
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="bg-mascp-light">
  <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 md:px-8 py-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-heading text-mascp-dark mb-8">Learn More</h2>
    <div class="md:flex md:gap-12">

      <div class="md:w-1/2 mb-8 md:mb-0">
        <h3 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-heading text-mascp-dark mb-2">VIVA COLCHA EMBROIDERY!</h3>
        <h4 class="text-lg md:text-xl font-heading text-mascp-dark mb-4">Needlework Tips and Techniques</h4>
        <p class="text-base md:text-lg leading-relaxed text-mascp-dark mb-4">
          The Spanish word colcha means coverlet or counterpane. New Mexicans typically call any bed covering a colcha. Textile enthusiasts use the word colcha to identify an embroidery stitch; or any finished piece in which the colcha stitch is used.
        </p>
        <a href="http://www.needlework-tips-and-techniques.com/colcha-embroidery.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-mascp-terracotta hover:text-mascp-red underline">Read More</a>
      </div>

      <div class="md:w-1/2">
        <h3 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-heading text-mascp-dark mb-2">
          <a href="http://www.cis-elsalvador.org/index.php/en/social-organizing/solidarity-crafts" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-mascp-terracotta hover:text-mascp-red">SOLIDARITY CRAFTS</a>
        </h3>
        <h4 class="text-lg md:text-xl font-heading text-mascp-dark mb-4">CIS - Centro de Intercambio y Solidaridad</h4>
        <p class="text-base md:text-lg leading-relaxed text-mascp-dark mb-4">
          CIS works with artists from marginalized backgrounds who are doing their best to improve their lives and communities. These artisans have formed cooperatives founded on the principles of fair wages, communal ownership, humane working conditions, and democratic participation.
        </p>
        <a href="http://www.cis-elsalvador.org/index.php/en/social-organizing/solidarity-crafts" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-mascp-terracotta hover:text-mascp-red underline">Read More</a>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>
